The automatic generation of a table of contents in a LATEX document can be done using the \tableofcontents command. This command will generate a list of all the sections and subsections in your document, with page numbers, so that it is easy to navigate to different parts of the document. You can also customize the appearance of the table of contents using various options, such as changing its font size or modifying the layout. For example:

\documentclass{article} 
\begin{document} 
\tableofcontents 
... 
\end{document}

